Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Polygonal hidden-line removal: the hiding pass hides the segments in
blocks beside each other on the threads of the default pool, and tests
each segment only against the hiding faces whose cells of a grid over the
view meet its own; the lines are the same, in the same order (mitcad#2021).

HLRBRep_PolyHLRToShape::Update hid every segment (a piece of an edge or
an outline, HLRAlgo_BiPoint) of every shell one after another on one
thread, even when only the visible lines are asked for. HLRAlgo_PolyAlgo::
Hide tested each segment's packed box against the box of every shell
and, for each shell whose box met it, every hiding face of that shell
(HLRAlgo_PolyData::HideByPolyData: the face's box, then each of its
triangles). The work grows with the segments times the shells, plus the
segments times the faces of the shells they meet; the boxes are those of
the 1020 x 1020 x 508 quantization of the whole view, so on a 6 m frame a
cell is about 6 mm and its long members meet many shells. A view of 884
bodies (39 966 faces) spent 7 to 9 s in that pass, the rest of the
projection about 4 s.

- HLRAlgo_PolyAlgo::Update keeps the segments in the order of InitHide
  and NextHide (NbSegments) and, for each hiding face, the cells of a grid
  of 128 x 128 (8 x 8 steps of the quantization in x and y) its box
  covers, its cells starting one step below its own in y: the packed box
  test passes a segment whose y reaches one step below the face's where
  the segment's depth reaches the face's (the depth's field carries into
  y's). A box outside the quantization (a face without hiding triangles)
  covers every cell. Each cell lists its faces in the order of the
  faces (shell by shell, a shell's hiding faces in order).
- HLRAlgo_PolyAlgo::HideSegment(theSegment, theWork, ...) const: Hide for
  one segment, with the work data of the calling thread (HidingWork: the
  triangle scratch and the candidate faces). The candidates are the faces
  listed in the cells the segment's box covers, each taken in the first
  cell both boxes share, sorted in the order of the faces; each is tested
  as Hide tested it: the box of its shell, then HideByPolyData with the
  same arguments. A face whose box test passes is always a candidate, and
  the faces hide the segment in the order in which the walk over the
  shells took them, so the edge status is Hide's. It writes nothing of
  the algorithm. Hide is HideSegment of the current segment.
- HLRBRep_PolyAlgo::NbSegments and HideSegment: the same, with the edge
  or face of the segment.
- HLRBRep_PolyHLRToShape::Update hides the segments in blocks of 64 on
  the default pool's threads (OSD_ThreadPool::Launcher, one HidingWork per
  thread), each block's visible and hidden lines in lists of its own,
  joined in the order of the blocks: the lists, and every compound made
  from them, are those of one segment after another.
- No catch is added; an exception in a block reaches the caller as the
  pool passes it on.

The patch's test and its before/after proof:
third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-patch-tests.md, section 1810.

Upstream: new; changes no result, the lines of every view are the same.

